This directory (`third-party/bt/`) contains a vendored fork of the "Bt" BitTorrent
client library, originally developed by Andrei Tomashpolskiy:

    https://github.com/atomashpolskiy/bt

The upstream project is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see the
`LICENSE` file in this directory). Every vendored Java source file retains its
original Apache license header and copyright notice.

Fork provenance
---------------
- Upstream version vendored: 1.10 (the sources of the Maven artifacts
  `com.github.atomashpolskiy:bt-bencoding:1.10` and `:bt-core:1.10`, extracted from
  the resolved `-sources.jar` files and imported unmodified).
- Modules vendored here: `bt-bencoding`, `bt-core` (re-namespaced to Maven group
  `org.blaze`; the Java packages remain `bt.*` so the fork is a drop-in replacement).
- Modules intentionally NOT vendored: `bt-dht` and `bt-http-tracker-client` stay as
  their upstream Maven artifacts. `bt-dht` shades a native `libmldht` engine and
  `bt-http-tracker-client` wraps the Apache HTTP client; neither hosts any Round-2
  feature, and both link against the fork through the unchanged `bt.*` API. Each is
  declared in `download-engine` with the upstream `bt-core`/`bt-bencoding` transitively
  excluded, so only this fork is on the classpath.
- blaze-dm modifies these sources for the download manager; every change is recorded
  in `PATCHES.md` in this directory, one reviewable commit per change.

